Title: AROS: read TrueType fonts into memory instead of keeping the file open
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: FreeType from the AROS SDK keeps a TrueType font file open with a DOS handle while the face exists, and a font that is still referenced when the program ends is never closed. After LibreSprite quit, data/fonts/font.ttf stayed "in use" until the next boot, so apkg remove kept the drawer and an upgrade could not replace the file.
Change: On AROS, ft::Lib::open reads the font file into a buffer owned by the Lib object (base::open_file, then FT_OPEN_MEMORY); the file is closed at once and the buffer is freed after FT_Done_FreeType.
Scope: AROS (all targets)
Upstream: local-only
Verification: builds without warnings for x86_64 ABIv11, mainline x86_64 and Raspberry Pi. ABIv11 (AROS One, pool v11-3, 2026-11-16): before, Delete of font.ttf after quitting gave "object is in use"; with this patch, the same steps (start, script prompts, New File dialog, quit) and Delete reports the file deleted.
Removal: when LibreSprite releases every font before exit, or the SDK FreeType closes its streams at exit.
---
diff --git a/src/ft/lib.h b/src/ft/lib.h
index e7f7a6114d756cffe4b93507518ae7a9389dea63..024a16faefd1db68b6c30aefac4d9c487a5f4040 100644
--- a/src/ft/lib.h
+++ b/src/ft/lib.h
@@ -9,8 +9,17 @@
 #include "base/disable_copying.h"
 #include "ft/freetype_headers.h"
 
+#include <cstring>
 #include <string>
 
+#ifdef __AROS__
+#include "base/file_handle.h"
+
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <list>
+#include <vector>
+#endif
+
 namespace ft {
 
   class Lib {
@@ -31,8 +40,21 @@ namespace ft {
     FT_Face open(const std::string& filename) {
       FT_Open_Args args;
       memset(&args, 0, sizeof(args));
+#ifdef __AROS__
+      // FreeType keeps the font file open while the face exists, with a
+      // DOS file handle that is not closed when the program ends. Fonts
+      // that live until exit then stay "in use" until the next boot.
+      // Read the file into memory instead; the buffer lives as long as
+      // this library object, which outlives its faces.
+      if (!readFile(filename))
+        return nullptr;
+      args.flags = FT_OPEN_MEMORY;
+      args.memory_base = m_buffers.back().data();
+      args.memory_size = FT_Long(m_buffers.back().size());
+#else
       args.flags = FT_OPEN_PATHNAME;
       args.pathname = (FT_String*)filename.c_str();
+#endif
 
       FT_Face face = nullptr;
       FT_Error err = FT_Open_Face(m_ft, &args, 0, &face);
@@ -42,6 +64,26 @@ namespace ft {
     }
 
   private:
+#ifdef __AROS__
+    bool readFile(const std::string& filename) {
+      base::FileHandle f = base::open_file(filename, "rb");
+      if (!f)
+        return false;
+      std::vector<FT_Byte> data;
+      FT_Byte chunk[16384];
+      size_t n;
+      while ((n = std::fread(chunk, 1, sizeof(chunk), f.get())) > 0)
+        data.insert(data.end(), chunk, chunk + n);
+      if (std::ferror(f.get()) || data.empty())
+        return false;
+      m_buffers.push_back(std::move(data));
+      return true;
+    }
+
+    // Freed after ~Lib() has run FT_Done_FreeType(), which closes the
+    // faces that read from these buffers.
+    std::list<std::vector<FT_Byte>> m_buffers;
+#endif
     FT_Library m_ft;
 
     DISABLE_COPYING(Lib);
